spectively. Amortization expense for intangible assets is included in depreciation and amortization in our condensed consolidated statements of operations. We did <ix:nonFraction unitRef="usd" contextRef="c-13" decimals="INF" name="us-gaap:ImpairmentOfIntangibleAssetsIndefinitelivedExcludingGoodwill" format="ixt:fixed-zero" scale="0" id="f-594"><ix:nonFraction unitRef="usd" contextRef="c-14" decimals="INF" name="us-gaap:ImpairmentOfIntangibleAssetsIndefinitelivedExcludingGoodwill" format="ixt:fixed-zero" scale="0" id="f-595"><ix:nonFraction unitRef="usd" contextRef="c-1" decimals="INF" name="us-gaap:ImpairmentOfIntangibleAssetsIndefinitelivedExcludingGoodwill" format="ixt:fixed-zero" scale="0" id="f-596"><ix:nonFraction unitRef="usd" contextRef="c-15" decimals="INF" name="us-gaap:ImpairmentOfIntangibleAssetsIndefinitelivedExcludingGoodwill" format="ixt:fixed-zero" scale="0" id="f-597">not</ix:nonFraction></ix:nonFraction></ix:nonFraction></ix:nonFraction> incur any intangible asset impairment charges for the three and six months ended June&#160;30, 2026 and 2025.</span></div><ix:continuation id="f-442-3"><div style="margin-bottom:3pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:18pt"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">As of December&#160;31, 2025, intangible assets consisted of the following (in thousands):</span></div><div style="margin-bottom:9pt;text-align:justify"><table style="border-collapse:collapse;display:inline-table;margin-bottom:5pt;vertical-align:text-bottom;width:100.000%"><tr><td style="width:1.0%"/><td style="width:55.470%"/><td style="width:0.1%"/><td style="width:1.0%"/><td style="width:12.842%"/><td style="width:0.1%"/><td style="width:0.1%"/><td style="width:0.601%"/><td style="width:0.1%"/><td style="width:1.0%"/><td style="width:12.842%"/><td style="width:0.1%"/><td style="width:0.1%"/><td style="width:0.601%"/><td style="width:0.1%"/><td style="width:1.0%"/><td style="width:12.844%